{
 "thread": "INjFKHPM5XY",
 "subject": "self joins for year-over-year analysis",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-03-15T03:58:17Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "-3HcMiDnDgAJ",
   "from": "Andrew Willis",
   "author": "38ec465044fe43d2",
   "date": "2017-03-14T13:13:46Z",
   "subject": "self joins for year-over-year analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am commonly working with data that has a value for every day, and I would like to do year-over-year comparisons. What&#39;s the best way to do a self join in order to grab &quot;earlier&quot; data from the same tibble?<div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example tibble:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tribble</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">same_day_last_year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20170313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">180</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160314&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20170312&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160314&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20150316&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">95</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20150315&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div></div><div>I would like to be able to join this tibble with itself so I can add a new column that shows the value from the same day last year.</div><div><br></div><div>Any pointers?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>Thanks!</div><div>-Andrew</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "VISZ_sXsDgAJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2017-03-14T14:57:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: self joins for year-over-year analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Andrew, <div><br></div><div>What you want is only sort of clear to me.</div><div><br></div><div>You seem to want to join a table with itself (hence &quot;self_join&quot;), but I&#39;m not sure that makes a lot of sense. </div><div><br></div><div>If you simply want to take a value minus the previous value you should consider a lag: <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/window-functions.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/window-functions.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357126023000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1GCw2ZebsD3ydvJexHcHV_\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/dplyr/vignettes/window-functions.html</a></div><div><br></div><div>If you want to take values from two tables and subtract them then you should have two tables, each with a date column and a value column. </div><div><br></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">library(tidyverse)</font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">library(lubridate)</font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">firstyear &lt;- tibble(date = as.Date(as.Date(&quot;2011-06-30&quot;):as.Date(&quot;2011-07-04&quot;), origin=&quot;1970-01-01&quot;), value = runif(5))<br></font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">secondyear &lt;-tibble(date = as.Date(as.Date(&quot;2012-06-30&quot;):as.Date(&quot;2012-07-04&quot;), origin=&quot;1970-01-01&quot;), value = runif(5))<br></font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\"># convert date to joinable numerics</font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">firstyear &lt;- </font></div><div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">firstyear %&gt;%</font></div></blockquote></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">mutate(month = month(date), day = day(date))<br></font></div></blockquote></div></blockquote><div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">secondyear &lt;- </font></div><div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">secondyear %&gt;%</font></blockquote></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">mutate(month = month(date), day = day(date))<br><br></font></blockquote></blockquote><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\"># look at join<br>full_join(firstyear, secondyear, by = c(&quot;month&quot;, &quot;day&quot;)) %&gt;%<br></font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\"># subtract firstyear$value from secondyear$value</font></div><div><font size=\"1\" face=\"comic sans ms, sans-serif\">mutate(subtractedvalue = value.y - value.x)</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>B</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Mar 14, 2017 at 6:13 AM, Andrew Willis <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andrew...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am commonly working with data that has a value for every day, and I would like to do year-over-year comparisons. What&#39;s the best way to do a self join in order to grab &quot;earlier&quot; data from the same tibble?<div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example tibble:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tribble</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">same_day_last_year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20170313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">180</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160314&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20170312&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160314&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20150316&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20160313&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">95</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;20150315&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div></div><div>I would like to be able to join this tibble with itself so I can add a new column that shows the value from the same day last year.</div><div><br></div><div>Any pointers?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>Thanks!</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div>-Andrew</div></font></span></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;manipulatr&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">manipulatr+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">manip...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357126023000&amp;usg=AOvVaw085OhT-aBzrn5IO0PenNkp\">https://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357126023000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2U1K2fMCfWRL0MP0sAQyRU\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
